// Title: Esentutl Volume Shadow Copy Service Keys
// Sigma ID: 5aad0995-46ab-41bd-a9ff-724f41114971
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez (Cyb3rWard0g), OTR (Open Threat Research)
// Date: 2020-10-20 | Modified: 2022-12-25
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.002
// Description: Detects the volume shadow copy service initialization and processing via esentutl. Registry keys
//   such as HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\VSS\\Diag\\VolSnap\\Volume are captured.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1003.002/T1003.002.md#atomic-test-3---esentutlexe-sam-copy
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_event_esentutl_volume_shadow_copy_service_keys.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey contains "System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\VSS" and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "esentutl.exe") and (not(RegistryKey contains "System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\VSS\\Start"))
